statement:
Implement a quantum oracle on N qubits which checks whether the number of bits equal to 1 in the input vector vecx is divisible by 3 (i.e., implements the function f(vecx) = 1 if the number of x_i = 1 in vecx is divisible by 3, and 0 otherwise).

You have to implement an operation which takes the following inputs:

and performs a transformation |xrangle|yrangle → |xrangle|y oplus f(x)rangle. The operation doesn't have an output; its "output" is the state in which it leaves the qubits. Note that the input register x has to remain unchanged after applying the operation.

Your code should have the following signature:

```
namespace Solution {
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Primitive;
    open Microsoft.Quantum.Canon;

    operation Solve (x : Qubit[], y : Qubit) : Unit {
        body (...) {
            // your code here
        }
        adjoint auto;
    }
}
```

Note: the operation has to have an adjoint specified for it; adjoint auto means that the adjoint will be generated automatically. For details on adjoint, see Operation Declarations.

You are not allowed to use measurements in your operation.
